From: Tamizh Chelvam Raja <tamizhr@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 26 May 2025 18:29:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: notify drivers about AP VLAN data offload

AP_VLAN interfaces normally have no firmware object, so mac80211 hides
their lifecycle and translates station callbacks to the parent AP.  A
driver which gives each AP_VLAN a hardware datapath object needs the
original interface for allocation and 4-address peer routing.

Add an opt-in hardware flag for that contract.  Notify capable drivers
when an AP_VLAN is opened, closed and restored, and preserve the AP_VLAN
for the 4-address callback and the authorization transition.  Restore
parent-first ordering during reconfiguration so a VLAN callback can safely
refer to its master.

When a station moves away from a 4-address VLAN, notify the old interface
before changing sta->sdata.  This prevents a hardware peer route from
remaining attached to the old VLAN while a new route is installed.

Based-on: ba31901cc92e3aa4aa2799876745af447b8a8bae
Link: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/system/feeds/wlan-open/-/blob/1ee3a4ab7c59ceaff347c4668fc6c7604a04c323/patches/ath12k/0337-10-QSDK-DP-wifi-Enable-DS-support-for-WDS-AP_VLAN-inter.patch
Signed-off-by: Tamizh Chelvam Raja <tamizhr@qti.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Balamurugan Mahalingam <bmahalin@qti.qualcomm.com>
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
